# Security, RBAC, and Audit

## Accounts

- Individual named accounts only — no shared user accounts.
- Passwords must be hashed with Django’s password hashers.
- Prefer session authentication for the browser/PWA application unless an approved ADR changes that.

## Authorization

- Deny access by default.
- Enforce authorization server-side in policies/services — never rely on UI hiding alone.
- Roles must be scoped (site, department, or equivalent confirmed hierarchy).
- Enforce separation of duties for create/check/verify and similar conflicting actions.

## Sessions and browser security

- Use secure cookie settings appropriate to each environment.
- CSRF protection remains enabled for cookie-authenticated mutating requests.
- Apply rate limiting for authentication and other abuse-sensitive endpoints when implemented.

## Secrets and access

- No secrets in source control.
- Restrict production access; privileged access must be reviewable.
- Do not write directly to ERP databases from this system.

## Audit

- Important operations must create audit events.
- Evidence access must be controlled and auditable.
- Prefer short-lived signed URLs for object-storage evidence delivery.

## Testing

- Every security and workflow authorization rule must have automated tests.
